  "dataExportFieldsText": "- kcal: kilocalories. P, C, F: protein, carbohydrates, fat in grams.\n- Goal: kcal and macro goal of the day. Training days have a higher kcal goal, rest days a lower one, so the week stays on target.\n- Pause day: a day without a goal, for example when ill or on holiday.\n- TDEE: estimated daily energy use, learned from weight and food, as in Progress. Training is already part of it; training days only move the day's goal.\n- Daily value: the TDEE that the smoothed food and the weight trend of the day imply, before the TDEE's ramp-up and daily cap; it swings a lot, and the TDEE follows it slowly.\n- Weight: weighing of the day; trend: smoothed weight.\n- Parts of the day: how the day's kcal goal splits over the meals.",
